WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:24.600
Bran Stark (the kid who tells everyone throughout
season 7 and 8 that he cannot be a lord of

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.720
anything because he is the three-eyed raven
now) is okay with becoming a king

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.610
and most people think Bran is this good guy
who is the best choice to lead Westeros into

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.620
a better future.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.550
Bran who claims he's this powerful Three Eyed
Raven who can see everything,

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.420
who can warg into others and who can travel
through the time, does nothing throughout

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.530
season 8?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.310
But what if I tell you Bran is the ultimate
villain of Game of Thrones, the ultimate evil

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.980
who used his abilities to orchestrate the
entire season 8, made Dany go mad, allowed

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.450
Kings Landing and its 1 million people to
burn alive, all so he, the Three-Eyed Raven

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.370
could end up on the Throne.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.900
Season 8 Episode 6 made it clear that Bran
knew everything that would happen,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.300
but didn’t do anything to change it or prevent
it.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.080
When Tyrion asked Bran if he would accept
to be their King,

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.650
Bran replies with “Why do you think I came
all the way here?”

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.650
Later in the episode when Jon Snow says farewell
to his family,

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.440
Jon apologizes to Bran for not being there
for him when he needed him,

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.790
on which Bran replied with “You were exactly
where you were supposed to be.”

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:24.220
Jon, Tyrion, Daenerys and the rest of the
characters were all chess pieces to him

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.720
that he used to get what he wants – the
Throne.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.259
Bran could have told Dany not to go to Dragonstone
back in episode 4 and warn her that Euron

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:34.810
is there waiting for her, but he chose not
to tell her.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:35.810
Why?

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:40.340
Because he knew Dany was going to lose another
child Rhaegal and closest friend Missandei,

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.280
and all of that matched with his plan.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.710
Bran knew everything but chose to tell only
as much as it benefits his ultimate goal.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.340
He manipulated things to turn exactly how
we saw it in season 8.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.610
Bran is the reason Dany went Mad Queen, and
he’s the reason Dany died.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:58.730
This was confirmed when Bran told to Jon “you
were exactly where you were supposed to be”,

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:02.730
which is sad to me because Dany definitely
did not deserve any of this.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:06.740
If not for Dany all these Starks including
Jon as well wouldn’t be alive at this point.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.620
If Dany was not so good-hearted and if she
was this Mad Queen all along, she wouldn’t

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.400
go north and help the Starks defend their
ancestral home and kingdom.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.990
But she did, she helped them and she saved
them.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:22.510
She lost a big portion of her armies and friends
in the process and what did she get in return?

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.270
The Starks forming an ultimate plan how to
make her mad, get her murdered and win the

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.440
Game of Thrones.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.200
Bran Stark is the ultimate villain.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.489
Littlefinger and Varys were right when they
said “knowledge is power”, and the one

00:02:32.489 --> 00:02:34.790
with most knowledge (Bran) wins.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.380
Bran knows everything that’s happened, everything
that’s happening, and everything that will

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.380
happen.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:56.959
Bran, the good honorable Stark died in that
cave and became the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:02:56.959 --> 00:03:16.410
When Benjen comes in out of nowhere and rescues
Bran and Meera, Meera asks Benjen why did

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:20.140
he rescue them,
he answered because the Three-Eyed Raven requested

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.140
him.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.010
When Meera counters that with saying that
the three-eyed raven just died, Benjen answered

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.349
''he lives again'',
confirming Bran is the three-eyed raven

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:34.349
which Bran confirmed himself over and over
again in seasons 7 and 8.

00:03:34.349 --> 00:03:35.810
Why is this important to highlight?

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.730
Well, because every Three-Eyed Ravens that
ever existed and the current three-eyed raven

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:44.150
as well, Bran, has the ability of greensight
which gives you the power to perceive the

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:48.000
past, present and future
through visions and time travel with ease.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.040
Bran already had great power and could see
future before even becoming the Three-Eyed

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.790
Raven,
of course not as clearly as he could later

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.250
on, but still he had that power.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.930
Remember back in season 2, Bran had strange
dreams that he would talk about with Osha.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:05.590
This time he reveals her a dream about the
sea flooding Winterfell and drowning Winterfell

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:10.120
and its people, even going as far to highlight
Ser Rodrik Cassel especially.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.510
Indeed, soon after that, Winterfell is attacked
by Theon Greyjoy and the Iron Born.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.340
Rodrick is captured and beheaded.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:21.030
Osha then tells Bran that his dream came true,
the Iron Islands (represented as the sea in

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:24.890
the dream) have come to Winterfell with their
Drowned god to drown it.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.270
Someone who also had the ability of greensight
was Jojen Reed

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.450
and he already knew how to see it clearly.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.210
When explaining the greensight to Bran he
tells him that they are visions of the past,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.210
present and future.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:39.720
We see how clear Jojen can see the future
when he brushes off the threats to kill him

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.560
of Nights Watch traitors while being captured
at Craster's Keep, saying he has already seen

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.900
his death in a vision and it won't be now,
as he sees a vision of his hand on fire.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:53.169
Indeed, he died by fire when they reached
the Three-Eyed Ravens cave.

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:56.419
Why I'm telling you all of this is just for
you to understand that Bran,

00:04:56.419 --> 00:05:00.840
who grew far more powerful than Jojen, Bran
was definitely able to see everything that

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:04.919
was going to happen in the future, he's seen
it all play out before it did.

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:08.550
Bran knew the Night King would come to him
and he knew Arya would come and save him.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.930
That's why he gave her Valyrian steel dagger.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:15.810
Bran started seeing glimpses of past and future
in season 4, something which Bran drastically

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.960
improved over the years, especially after
becoming the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.100
Bran saw Drogon flying above Kings Landing
about to burn it down and even saw the aftermath

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.669
of Drogon and his burning of Kings Landing.

00:05:26.669 --> 00:05:31.050
All of this he saw from his first vision ever,
which was a long time ago when he wasn’t

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.650
as powerful as he is now years later.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.130
This was much before he even became the Three-Eyed
Raven.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:40.320
He also saw a wildfire vision before Cersei
blew the Sept of Baelor.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.550
Not only is it safe to say, but this is an
actual evidence supporting the fact that Bran

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.599
knew
what would happen to Kings Landing before

00:05:46.599 --> 00:05:49.310
it actually happened, but chose to not change
anything,

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:53.610
chose to stay silent and chose 1 million people
to die, all so he could become the king.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:56.039
Everyone from Arya to Jon were just puppets
for Bran

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:58.510
and he used them to orchestrate the end we’ve
got.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:01.900
Bran orchestrated the deaths of the Night
King as well as of Dany

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.990
and ensured he would end up on the Throne.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.061
Bran isn’t Bran Stark anymore, Bran died
in that Cave

00:06:07.061 --> 00:06:11.410
when the old three-eyed Raven transferred
his own mind to Bran's he is the Three-Eyed

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.819
Raven
and his only goal was to end on the Iron Throne

00:06:13.819 --> 00:06:18.039
through the power of seeing past, present
and future, through orchestrating future events

00:06:18.039 --> 00:06:21.650
which he did by carefully choosing what to
say and what not to say.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.590
The Night King wasn't coming after all humanity,
he was coming for the Three-Eyed Raven which

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:50.930
Bran confirmed in season 8 episode 3.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:54.790
Bran says he is coming for him because he
is worlds memory and the Night King wants

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:59.099
to erase worlds memory, but I am convinced
the Night King was coming for this three-eyed

00:06:59.099 --> 00:07:02.410
raven
to save humanity from such great evil taking

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.349
over, but he failed.

00:07:04.349 --> 00:07:08.289
The first future event Bran orchestrated was
the fall of the Night King by giving Arya

00:07:08.289 --> 00:07:12.300
the Valyrian steel dagger which he knew Arya
would later use to kill the Night King in

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.060
that very same spot.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:18.129
In the Game of Thrones among the living though,
Bran was as useless as he could get

00:07:18.129 --> 00:07:19.150
but he actually wasn't.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.540
It's a fact that Bran can see the future and
manipulate it.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.389
Bran's visions prove it, the ending proves
it, and Bran confirms it by saying ''why do

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:30.819
you think I came all this way''
to Tyrion when he asks him if he will be their

00:07:30.819 --> 00:07:31.819
king.

00:07:31.819 --> 00:07:35.611
But let's imagine Bran cannot see the future
and those glimpses of the future that he can

00:07:35.611 --> 00:07:38.530
see
and what he saw are truly only glimpses

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.000
and he cannot use them to tell what’s going
to happen

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.669
which definitely isn’t because he kind of
confirmed he can see and orchestrate the future

00:07:44.669 --> 00:07:48.820
by giving Arya the Valyrian steel dagger
on the same place that would later be used

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:53.129
to kill the Night King and by telling Tyrion
that he knew he would be chosen a king

00:07:53.129 --> 00:07:56.450
and by telling Jon that he was exactly where
he was supposed to be.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.380
David Benioff also said that Bran said “thank
you” to Theon

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:03.920
because Bran knew what was going to happen,
kind of confirming that Bran has seen everything

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.009
and knows everything that’s going to happen
in the future.

00:08:07.009 --> 00:08:09.360
But for the sake of the argument, let’s
say that’s true,

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:12.229
let’s say Bran cannot see and orchestrate
the future.

00:08:12.229 --> 00:08:16.039
It still doesn’t change a fact that he could
have prevented the burning of Kings Landing.

00:08:16.039 --> 00:08:48.410
Bran said it himself that he can see everything
that’s happened and everything that is happening.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.040
So why didn’t he warg into Dany or Drogon
and stopped that madness

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.100
and prevent 1 million people from dying?

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:58.380
Or why didn’t he warn Dany that Euron is
waiting for her at Dragonstone, preventing

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.780
him from killing Dany’s dragon and best
friend?

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.680
He was there at the war council just before
she went to Dragonstone.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.630
Oh yes, I forgot, it all had to happen, it
was in fact orchestrated by Bran so he could

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.630
get the Throne...

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.200
Bran’s been manipulating events throughout
the entire season 8 that would get him to

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.200
this point.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.360
Bran is the final villain of the story.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.980
Bran manipulated Sam into telling Jon the
truth

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:39.720
specifically after Dany had just told Sam
she'd burned his father and brother alive.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.930
Bran did this on purpose knowing Sam would
not only reveal to Jon the truth,

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:48.070
but also tell Jon that she is not the best
choice for the people of Westeros,

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:51.870
but more importantly, Bran knew Jon wouldn't
continue his relationship with Dany after

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:56.730
finding out the truth and Dany would become
more paranoid after learning Jon has the best

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.140
claim to the throne.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:01.820
And let's face it, that's the only reason
Jon found out the truth about his parents

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:06.571
Rhaegar and Lyanna, only so Jon would end
his relationship with Dany and wouldn't give

00:10:06.571 --> 00:10:11.430
Dany the affection she needed after losing
her children, her armies and her advisors.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.700
The only thing it would give Dany is paranoia.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.460
Bran also knew that Jon was going to tell
the truth to his family, Arya and Sansa,

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:21.140
and Bran knew Sansa didn’t like Dany and
she’s Littlefinger’s student.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:25.580
He knew Sansa would start scheming to overthrow
Dany by using Jon’s claim -- and he knew

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:29.680
that this way the truth behind Jon’s true
parentage and the claim would spread.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:34.320
Bran tells to Sam to tell the truth to Jon,
Jon tells the truth to his family, Sansa tells

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:38.950
it to Tyrion, Tyrion tells it to Varys and
Varys informs all the seven kingdoms.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.950
The truth spreads, Dany’s own advisors start
plotting behind her back,

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.450
which makes Dany grow more and more paranoid.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:49.450
Bran deliberately doesn't warn Dany how Euron
is waiting for her at Dragonstone

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:53.950
even though he can see everything, which leads
to Dany losing Rhaegal and Missandei,

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:58.390
all of this making Dany more frustrated and
ultimately turning her mad which leads to

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:01.410
her burning the entire city and all the innocent.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:05.920
Jon is then left with no choice, but to kill
her and Jon himself must be punished for this.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.010
Also, that scene where Jaime asks Bran why
didn’t he tell everyone else what he did

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:14.090
to him, on which Bran replies “you wouldn’t
be able to help us in this fight if I let

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:21.630
them murder 
you first”.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:25.519
Jaime didn’t do anything of great importance
in the battle for Winterfell,

00:11:25.519 --> 00:11:28.029
he did not have any role in killing the Night
King,

00:11:28.029 --> 00:11:31.450
he did not kill any White Walkers which would
reduce the Night King’s army during the

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.450
battle.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.740
All he did was fighting wights, like everyone
else in the living army.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:40.850
So he did not help at all during this fight,
at least not more than any other soldier.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.589
He did something significant in the other
fight though,

00:11:43.589 --> 00:11:47.790
the fight for Kings Landing when he rang the
hell bells that for some reason made Dany

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.830
go crazy,
so that must have been the help Bran saw Jaime

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:54.339
would provide in the future,
also seemingly seeing that right after this,

00:11:54.339 --> 00:12:01.260
he would be killed by bricks.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:05.280
All the events Bran manipulated led to the
outcome he’s been working on this entire

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.730
season,
Bran Stark becomes the King.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:10.550
Bran, the one with the most knowledge and
thus the most power,

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:11.950
wins the Game of Thrones.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.970
He was behind everything that happened in
season 8.

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:18.350
Not so bad of an ending after all -- if it
was well written

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.940
and if Bran had any other line other than
“I don’t want anything really.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:25.780
I can’t be the lord of Winterfell I’m
the three-eyed raven now” and if the execution

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:28.990
was not so terrible
and if only they did not make Dany go from

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:33.019
the ultimate savior to the ultimate mad queen
in the span of 1 episode.

00:12:33.019 --> 00:12:35.162
In fact, it’s how George RR Martin’s books
will also end

00:12:35.162 --> 00:12:38.570
as they said multiple times that the ending
will be the same,

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.230
but the journey to get there will be quite
different,

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.440
and the journey is exactly what was so disappointing
here.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.790
In the books, we already have clues that Bran,
the Three-Eyed Raven is evil.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:52.580
One of the visions Melisandre sees in the
flames is about a 'wooden face, corpse white'

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:56.850
with a thousand red eyes accompanied by a
boy with a wolfs face,

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:59.580
and Melisandre wonders if this is THE enemy.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:04.160
Her vision is obviously about the old three-eyed
raven teaching Bran how to become him

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.579
and she seems to think they are the real enemy.

00:13:06.579 --> 00:13:09.221
Anyways, Dany going mad, Bran becoming the
King,

00:13:09.221 --> 00:13:13.290
and everything else could have been written
so that all of this would make sense.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.380
More importantly, it should not have been
rushed,

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:19.240
there should have been more episodes and more
seasons to wrap it all up nicely.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:36.760
Even HBO knew it and offered Dan and David
unlimited budget to do 10 seasons, which they

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:40.730
refused.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:58.380
Instead, we got 

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:03.259
rushed and poorly written season where the
ending is nowhere near bittersweet, only bitter.

00:14:03.259 --> 00:14:08.410
Bran did learn how to see things better and
what did he choose to do with the information?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:12.820
He chose to sit in his wheelchair, sacrifice
everyone else,

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:16.260
orchestrate things and events to lead him
and his family into ultimate victory in the

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.399
Game of Thrones.

00:14:17.399 --> 00:14:22.019
They chose an evil man to be their king, a
guy who manipulated the entire plot just to

00:14:22.019 --> 00:14:23.019
be a king.

00:14:23.019 --> 00:14:28.150
''Why do you think I came all this way'' disgusts
me, it disgusts me that he knew it all along.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:32.070
What a great king Westeros has right now,
a king that did not care to stop Dany from

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:35.040
burning down Kings Landing and killing 1 million
people.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:39.230
Bran manipulated the events to make Dany mad
so Jon would be forced to kill her.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:43.190
This way Dany is obviously dead and cannot
be the Queen while Jon takes the black for

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.980
killing her
which makes him no longer a legitimate heir

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.199
to the throne.

00:14:47.199 --> 00:14:51.600
Only after this - Bran decided to reveal that
he knew and saw all this play out already

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:56.500
as he orchestrated it all by telling some
little, but more importantly not telling more.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:00.890
Bran basically used his all-seeing ability
of past, present, and future to help only

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:03.850
him and his family
(not including Jon Snow because as he said

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:08.470
himself, he doesn't see Jon as his brother),
ensuring his family comes at the top at the

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:13.100
end, instead of using it at all for the benefit
of others to save others... if you ask me,

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:16.650
that makes Bran Stark the ultimate villain
of Game of Thrones.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:31.660
No human rules the Six Kingdoms, The Three-Eyed
Raven does.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:37.420
The final episode of Game of Thrones and Bran's
two responses,

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:41.380
firstly to Tyrion when asked if he would like
to be their king ''why do you think I came

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:45.630
